Hello,
i installed 4.10 on alpha.
With 4.9 I had not this problem.
When i try to install linux base and the linux ldconfig is executed
I have a unaligned kernel trap and the system reboots.
this happens when glibc-2.2.4-32.1.alpha.rpm is processed by ports 
installation.
I have no problem when loading the linux emulation module.
the problem occours when the linux base ldconfig is executed.
is there any way to make the kernel ignore the kernel trap?
I tryed changing the default values of
machdep.unaligned_print: 1
machdep.unaligned_fix: 1
machdep.unaligned_sigbus: 0
but I Solved nothing.
any hints ?
this happens to me since the new 4.10 release has been installed

thanks

Rick


