Running "/usr/sbin/periodic daily" reliably locks up my PC164 with
5.2-CURRENT from June 13.  (A June 15 kernel would already lock up
while going multiuser.)  It doesn't panic, it doesn't crash into
SRM, it just locks up.  After a reset the machine gets stuck in SRM
self test; it needs to be power-cycled.

I suspect it's nothing in daily itself but rather all the forking/
execing.  (sh -x didn't show any likely culprit.)

-- 
